# Project Knowledge Configuration

**SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH** for knowledge-base paths. Other rules (`lookup-order`, `knowledge-capture`) and skills MUST use the variables below — do **not** hardcode project folder names like `Onboarding` in agent workflows.

## Variables to edit when switching projects

Edit **only these two** in this file (and mirror `PROJECT_NAME` / `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` in `PROJECT_KB_ROOT/PROJECT.md`):

| Variable | Current value | Purpose |
|----------|---------------|---------|
| `PROJECT_NAME` | `Onboarding` | Product / knowledge-base project id |
| `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` | `d:\VibeCoding\Projects\Onboarding` | Project-specific 2nd Brain (playbooks, runbooks, Docker, versioning) |

## Derived variables (do not edit — compute from above)

Agents MUST resolve these from `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` / layout; never leave them pointing at an old project.

| Variable | Resolved as |
|----------|-------------|
| `PROJECT_KB_README` | `{PROJECT_KB_ROOT}\README.md` |
| `COMMON_FROM_PROJECT` | `../../Common` (relative from `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` → `COMMON_KB_ROOT`) |

Example: if `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` = `d:\VibeCoding\Projects\ProductX`, then `PROJECT_KB_README` = `d:\VibeCoding\Projects\ProductX\README.md`.

## Shared / workspace variables (usually unchanged)

| Variable | Current value | Purpose |
|----------|---------------|---------|
| `COMMON_KB_ROOT` | `d:\VibeCoding\Common` | Shared knowledge (specs, coding rules, commit rules) — all projects |
| `CODE_REPO_ROOT` | `d:\SourceCode\BIOS_Project\EDK2_0526\edk2` | This edk2 workspace (firmware source) |
| `CODE_REPO_URL` | `https://github.com/Vincent04190609/edk2.git` | Git remote for this code repo |

## Two-Layer Knowledge Model

| Layer | Root | Contains |
|-------|------|----------|
| **Common** | `COMMON_KB_ROOT` | UEFI / SMBIOS / ACPI specs, `Coding-Rule/`, `Commit-Rule/`, industry standards |
| **Project** | `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` | `development-guides/`, `playbooks/`, `runbooks/`, `DockerImage/`, `VersionList.xlsx`, project architecture |

## WSL Path Resolution (MANDATORY for agents running in WSL/Linux)

`PROJECT_KB_ROOT` and `COMMON_KB_ROOT` are stored as Windows paths. Agents running in WSL **MUST** convert to POSIX before any file I/O or Python operation:

| Windows path | WSL/Linux equivalent |
|---|---|
| `d:\VibeCoding\Projects\Onboarding` | `/mnt/d/VibeCoding/Projects/Onboarding` |
| `d:\VibeCoding\Common` | `/mnt/d/VibeCoding/Common` |

**Rule**: Replace `d:\` → `/mnt/d/`, then replace all `\` → `/`. Never pass a `d:\...` path to a Linux process (Python, shell, openpyxl, etc.).

## How Agents Resolve Paths

1. **Project workflows** → compute `PROJECT_KB_README`, read it, then use paths under `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` (converted to WSL form if on Linux).
2. **Standards** → `COMMON_KB_ROOT` or `COMMON_FROM_PROJECT` from project docs.
3. **Write-back** → only under `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` unless updating Common standards.
4. **Markdown in project KB** → relative paths (`./development-guides/...`, `../../Common/...`).

## Changing to Another Project

1. Edit **`PROJECT_NAME`** and **`PROJECT_KB_ROOT`** in this file only.
2. Update `PROJECT.md` at the new `PROJECT_KB_ROOT` (copy from another project if needed).
3. Open the matching edk2 code workspace; update `CODE_REPO_ROOT` / `CODE_REPO_URL` here if that clone differs.
4. `lookup-order` / `knowledge-capture` need no changes — they reference this file.

See also: `project-prd.mdc` (repo setup, PR protocol), `project-prd-org.md` (full PRD).
